UID:feminist-gaming-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
SUMMARY:Deadline: Feminist Gaming Fellowship: Open Call 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Feminist Gaming Project is opening applications for its fir
 st Fellowship cohort: five fellows from different creative and research fi
 elds spending three months developing 3D assets\, tools\, and documentatio
 n for its Open Access Asset Library (OAL)\, a free\, open repository of in
 clusive 3D content created by\, with\, and for intersectionally feminist a
 nd diverse communities. Where mainstream marketplaces default to hyper-ath
 letic\, idealized\, or hyper-sexualized characters\, the OAL offers averag
 e bodies\, real postures\, everyday objects\, and the kinds of lives most 
 games leave out (pregnancy and postpartum\, care work\, ageing\, disabilit
 y\, domestic labor). This first cohort is dedicated to 3D content. Support
 ed by the Creative Industries Fund NL and working across the Netherlands\,
  Türkiye\, Germany\, and the UK\, the project challenges exclusionary nor
 ms in how games are made. The fellowship offers a EUR 1\,000 honorarium pe
 r fellow over three months (half at start\, half on completion)\; mentorsh
 ip from the core team and advisors in feminist design\, game studies\, 3D 
 production\, and digital culture\; a peer community across NL\, TR\, DE\, 
 and the UK with biweekly meetings\; visibility through a travelling exhibi
 tion program\, publications\, and public events\; and authorship credited 
 in the OAL under its license terms. Five roles are recruited (one fellow e
 ach): 3D Character Artist for inclusive base meshes\; 3D Character Artist 
 for pregnancy and postpartum assets\; 3D Animator for neutral and everyday
  movement\; 3D Modeller for domestic and care-labor environments\; and Res
 earcher/Writer for documentation and the representation framework\; applic
 ants may rank up to two. Open to 3D artists\, animators\, modellers\, desi
 gners\, researchers\, and writers committed to inclusive and intersectiona
 l representation in games\; prior game-industry experience is not required
 \, and emerging creators\, underrepresented practitioners\, and researcher
 s at the intersection of games\, gender\, and culture are especially encou
 raged\, particularly those based in or connected to NL\, TR\, DE\, or the 
 UK. To apply\, email feministgamingproject@gmail.com with a short statemen
 t (max ~500 words)\, a portfolio or work samples (a link is fine)\, and co
 nfirmation of availability for the three-month period\; name the role(s) i
 n the subject line or statement. The project explicitly asks applicants to
  write statements in their own voice rather than using AI-generated text. 
 Indicative timeline: applications close 12 July 2026\; selection and notif
 ication late July\; fellowship period August to October 2026\; showcase an
 d publication November to December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Feminist Gaming 
 Project\nLocation: Remote across the Netherlands\, Türkiye\, Germany\, an
 d the UK\nAward: EUR 1\,000 honorarium per fellow (paid half at the start\
 , half on completion)\nDuration: Three months\, August to October 2026\; m
 inimum ~6 hours per week (~75 hours total)\n\nMore: https://feministgaming
 .com/fellowship/index.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://feministgaming.com/fellowship/index.html?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote across the Netherlands\, Türkiye\, Germany\, and the UK
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ford-foundation-technology-fellow-digital-safety-security-2026@artifici
 alnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:Deadline: Technology Fellow: Digital Safety and Security
DESCRIPTION:The Ford Foundation seeks a two-year Technology Fellow for Digi
 tal Safety and Security to expand the foundation's ability to support gran
 tee digital safety and security. Civil society organizations face targeted
  information security threats yet many lack the resources and training to 
 maintain robust digital security. Reporting to the Director\, Office of th
 e Vice President for U.S. Programs\, the Fellow will identify field-buildi
 ng opportunities in the public-interest digital safety and security field\
 , work directly with program officers across US and global teams to integr
 ate digital security capacity into Ford's technical assistance programs\, 
 provide strategic support to high-risk grantees\, and assess strategic gap
 s in the ecosystem for safety and security providers. The Technology Fello
 ws Program is administered by Ford's Technology and Society Program and is
  designed to increase sociotechnical capacity within the Foundation. Requi
 rements include a minimum of 7 years' professional experience with media\,
  technology\, advocacy or policy organizations\; a baccalaureate degree or
  equivalent experience\; sophisticated knowledge of existing and emerging 
 technologies with a focus on surveillance technologies and organizational 
 digital safety and security\; and experience designing\, implementing or s
 upporting digital safety and security solutions in a complex global settin
 g. Hybrid role based in New York (three days per week in office) with appr
 oximately 10 to 20 percent domestic and international travel. Not eligible
  for visa sponsorship\; candidates must be authorized to work in the Unite
 d States. Submit both a resume and a cover letter to be considered.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Ford Foundation\nLocation: New York\, New York\, USA\nAward: US
 D 166\,000 to 170\,000 annual salary\, plus comprehensive benefits and ret
 irement contributions of up to 13%\nDuration: Two-year term-limited contra
 ct\n\nMore: https://fordfoundation.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/FordFoundat
 ionCareerPage/details/Technology-Fellow--Digital-Safety-and-Security_R1295
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fordfoundation.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/FordFoundationCareer
 Page/details/Technology-Fellow--Digital-Safety-and-Security_R1295?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York\, New York\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ford-foundation-technology-fellow-ai-philanthropy-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:Deadline: Technology Fellow: AI and Philanthropy
DESCRIPTION:The Ford Foundation seeks a two-year Technology Fellow for AI a
 nd Philanthropy\, an internally-facing role focused on cross-programmatic 
 learning and advisory support. Reporting to the Director\, Technology and 
 Society\, the AI Tech Fellow will support Foundation staff in building and
  adapting internal frameworks for evaluating AI use in ways that prioritiz
 e mission and strategy and address ethical\, sociotechnical\, and operatio
 nal considerations. Responsibilities include designing and curating hands-
 on trainings\, workshops\, and learning sessions to help staff build pract
 ical familiarity with AI tools and critically assess their value and effic
 acy\; creating accessible documentation and guides on mission-aligned AI e
 xperimentation\; curating sociotechnical conversations on how philanthropy
  and the nonprofit sector are experimenting with AI in ways that respect p
 rivacy\, safety\, and equity\; monitoring emerging global AI developments 
 and providing timely briefings to program teams\; conducting landscape res
 earch on AI initiatives in the philanthropy and social justice sectors\; a
 nd building relationships with AI researchers\, practitioners\, grantees a
 nd partners working on mission-enabling AI. The Technology Fellows Program
  is administered by Ford's Technology and Society Program and is designed 
 to increase sociotechnical capacity within the Foundation. Requirements in
 clude a minimum of 7 years working within public-interest\, government\, c
 ivil society\, or commercial technology sectors\; a baccalaureate degree o
 r equivalent experience\; demonstrated sociotechnical expertise in artific
 ial intelligence and related technologies including machine learning syste
 ms and generative AI and their societal implications\; and experience desi
 gning\, implementing or supporting AI applications and tools in a complex 
 global setting. Hybrid role based in New York (three days per week in offi
 ce). Not eligible for visa sponsorship\; candidates must be authorized to 
 work in the United States. Submit both a resume and a cover letter to be c
 onsidered.\n\nOrganisation: Ford Foundation\nLocation: New York\, New York
 \, USA\nAward: USD 166\,000 to 170\,000 annual salary\, plus comprehensive
  benefits and retirement contributions of up to 13%\nDuration: Two-year te
 rm-limited contract\n\nMore: https://fordfoundation.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/
 en-US/FordFoundationCareerPage/details/Technology-Fellow--AI-and-Philanthr
 opy_R1294?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fordfoundation.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/FordFoundationCareer
 Page/details/Technology-Fellow--AI-and-Philanthropy_R1294?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York\, New York\, USA
END:VEVENT
