UID:insideout-refocus-fund-postproduction-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260723
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inside Out RE:Focus Fund Post-Production Grants 2026
DESCRIPTION:Established in 2018 through a lead gift from Martha McCain\, In
 side Out's RE:Focus Fund addresses industry inequities by providing direct
  financial support to women\, non-binary\, and/or trans filmmakers telling
  2SLGBTQ+ stories. Launched in 2019\, the RE:Focus Fund Post-Production Gr
 ants support the post-production and promotion of short and feature films.
  Applications for the 2026 round open 29 June 2026. ELIGIBILITY: women\, n
 on-binary\, and/or trans filmmakers whose projects tell 2SLGBTQ+ stories\;
  per the FAQ\, international projects may be eligible to apply. The reques
 ted funding amount is determined by the applicant\, and unsuccessful appli
 cants can request feedback and reapply the following year. Inside Out also
  runs other RE:Focus initiatives\, including a new Residency program for f
 irst-time feature filmmakers facing intersectional barriers. KEY DATES: su
 bmissions open 29 June 2026\, close 22 July 2026\, with notifications by 1
 5 August 2026. Apply and read the FAQ via the Eventival page linked from t
 he RE:Focus Fund site\; questions to industry@insideout.ca.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Inside Out (Toronto 2SLGBTQ+ Film Festival)\nLocation: Toronto\, Canada
  (Inside Out is a Canadian organisation\; international projects may apply
 \, see FAQ)\nAward: Post-production grant funding to support the completio
 n and promotion of short and feature films\; the requested amount is set b
 y the applicant (see the FAQ 'How much funding can I request?'). Since 201
 8 the RE:Focus Fund has distributed more than CAD 300\,000 in grants and p
 rograms. No application fee.\nDuration: One-off post-production grant\n\nM
 ore: https://insideout.ca/initiatives/re-focus-fund/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://insideout.ca/initiatives/re-focus-fund/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Toronto\, Canada (Inside Out is a Canadian organisation\; internat
 ional projects may apply\, see FAQ)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:loghaven-artist-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Loghaven Artist Residency
DESCRIPTION:Loghaven Artist Residency offers practicing artists time\, spac
 e\, and resources on ninety wooded acres in Knoxville\, Tennessee. Fellows
  stay in five rehabilitated historic log cabins with access to purpose-bui
 lt studio space. Each Fellow receives an USD 850 weekly living stipend\, a
  travel subsidy on a sliding scale from USD 400 to 800\, up to USD 200 in 
 materials shipping reimbursement\, and covered room and board. Residencies
  run from 2 to 6 weeks across sessions scheduled throughout 2027. The prog
 ram is open to artists at any career stage working in architecture\, dance
 \, interdisciplinary art\, music composition\, theater\, visual art\, and 
 writing\, including collaborative groups of up to nine people. Applicants 
 must be at least 21\, live more than 120 miles from Knoxville\, and be eli
 gible to work legally in the US\; international artists and degree-seeking
  students are not eligible.\n\nOrganisation: Loghaven Artist Residency\nLo
 cation: Knoxville\, Tennessee\, USA\nAward: USD 850 weekly living stipend\
 , travel subsidy USD 400 to 800\, up to USD 200 materials shipping reimbur
 sement\, plus room and board\, housing in historic log cabins\, and studio
  space USD 25 non-refundable application fee (fee waiver available on requ
 est)\nDuration: 2 to 6 weeks depending on session\n\nMore: https://loghave
 n.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://loghaven.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Knoxville\, Tennessee\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:center-for-fiction-emerging-writer-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Center for Fiction / Susan Kamil Emerging Writer Fell
 owship
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Fiction / Susan Kamil Emerging Writer Fellowship
  annually supports nine early-career\, New York City-based fiction writers
  at a pivotal point in their careers. Each fellow receives a 5\,000 USD gr
 ant\, dedicated space and time to write in the Writers Studio\, personaliz
 ed editorial mentorship\, opportunities to meet literary agents\, and comm
 unity programming. Applicants must be current residents of one of the five
  boroughs and must remain in New York City for the entire fellowship year.
  An emerging writer is defined as someone who has not yet had a novel or s
 hort story collection published by a major or independent publisher and wh
 o is not currently under contract for a work of fiction\; students enrolle
 d in a degree-granting program during the fellowship year are not eligible
 . The 2027 fellowship application window opens July 1\, 2026 and closes Ju
 ly 31\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: The Center for Fiction\nLocation: New York 
 City\, USA\nAward: USD 5\,000 grant plus writers studio space\, mentorship
 \, agent introductions\, and community programming\nDuration: One year (th
 e fellowship year)\n\nMore: https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/nyc
