DESCRIPTION:Request for proposals for ambitious AI-first projects that make
  the transition to capable AI go well and use it to unlock science. Three 
 layers: local compute that individuals or communities physically own and c
 ontrol\; coordination and accountability (supercollaboration and decentral
 ized alignment\, human empowerment\, AI insurance and open governance)\; a
 nd AI-first science in bio\, neuro and nano (automated nanotechnology\, wh
 ole-brain emulation\, replacement\, enhancement\, biostasis). Selected pro
 jects receive grant funding\, private local compute\, workspace at the San
  Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes\, travel-paid field-building events and acce
 ss to Foresight's advisors and scientific network. ELIGIBILITY: individual
 s\, teams and organisations worldwide\; applicants who want to be active i
 n-person contributors at the Nodes are strongly prioritised. Deadline 31 O
 ctober 2026\, 23:59 PDT.\n\nOrganisation: Foresight Institute\nLocation: R
 emote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)\nAward: Typically $30\,0
 00 to $100\,000 per grant (larger amounts possible for the right project)\
 , plus private local compute and workspace at the San Francisco or Berlin 
 AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\n\nMore: https://fo
 resight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
END:VEVENT
