UID:gifct-memberships-programs-internship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:Deadline: GIFCT: Internship\, Memberships & Programs
DESCRIPTION:GIFCT is hiring a part-time intern to support its Memberships a
 nd Programs team. Work spans three areas: open-source research and early h
 uman rights assessments on companies applying to the Membership Advisory P
 rogram\, reviewing them against GIFCT's Membership Criteria\; assisting th
 e annual member review process and mapping companies that could benefit fr
 om GIFCT tools\; and helping update the Definitions and Legislation Projec
 t with new case studies and resources. Generalist exposure to an organisat
 ion working at the intersection of technology\, trust and safety\, and cou
 nterterrorism policy\, including drafting communications\, records\, event
  logistics and reporting. Strong written and organisational skills require
 d\; interest in tech policy\, trust and safety\, human rights or internati
 onal security is a plus. Reports to Dr. Nagham El Karhili. Apply by emaili
 ng a resume plus answers to three short questions (in lieu of a cover lett
 er) to jobs@gifct.org with 'M&P Internship' in the subject line. NOTE: thi
 s is a paid internship\, not a grant or fellowship. Deadline 1 August 2026
 .\n\nOrganisation: Global Internet Forum to Counter Terrorism (GIFCT)\nLoc
 ation: Remote (preference for US Eastern timezone)\nAward: Paid role: $25/
 hour\, part-time at a maximum of 24 hours per week (3 days a week). No app
 lication fee.\nDuration: Mid-August to mid-December 2026\n\nMore: https://
 gifct.org/opportunities/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral#internship--memberships---programs
URL:https://gifct.org/opportunities/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral#internship--memberships---programs
LOCATION:Remote (preference for US Eastern timezone)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:forma-curator-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Forma: Curator (6-month contract)
DESCRIPTION:Forma\, a London contemporary art organisation commissioning ar
 tists who address social and political questions\, seeks an experienced cu
 rator to oversee delivery of its artistic programme for six months while t
 he organisation undertakes a strategic review. Reporting to the Artistic D
 irector\, you step into an existing programme of commissions\, exhibitions
 \, residencies and public events\, acting as the central point of contact 
 for artists\, partners and the Forma team\, and keeping production\, commu
 nications\, budgets and timelines aligned. PROGRAMME HIGHLIGHTS during the
  term: Scotland + Venice\, Bugarin + Castle's 'Shame Parade'\; Frieze Lond
 on Artist Award 2026\; Artists' Film International 2027\; the Forma Bermon
 dsey Square Gallery Winter/Spring exhibition\; and legacy planning and tou
 ring for Oliver Frank Chanarin's 'A Perfect Sentence'. RESPONSIBILITIES: c
 oordinate multiple concurrent projects\, maintaining project plans\, produ
 ction schedules and risk registers\; set and monitor programme and project
  budgets with the Artistic Director and Managing Director\; act as princip
 al day-to-day contact for artists\, curators and partners and coordinate c
 ontracts\, agreements and rights\; coordinate weekly delivery schedules\, 
 team updates and staffing across FormaHQ\; support the Creative Producer o
 n freelance technicians\, logistics\, health and safety\, and be present a
 t installation\, film shoots\, fabrication and live events\; co-curate exh
 ibitions\, screenings\, talks and performances at FormaHQ and Forma Bermon
 dsey Square\; and support the Marketing and Communications Manager\, draft
 ing exhibition texts\, press releases and editorial pieces. ESSENTIAL: cur
 ating contemporary visual art\, exhibition production\, managing artists\,
  budget and project management\, working with multiple partners\, excellen
 t administration\, calm under pressure\, strong written communication. DES
 IRABLE: international contemporary art networks\, public programme product
 ion\, touring exhibitions\, commissioning\, trust and foundation fundraisi
 ng\, Photoshop and InDesign. Forma particularly welcomes candidates underr
 epresented in the sector due to barriers linked to ethnicity\, class\, dis
 ability\, gender and sexuality\, and offers informal conversations in adva
 nce of the deadline (contact Caroline Heron\, ch@forma.org.uk). Apply via 
 the online form. NOTE: this is a paid job\, not a grant or fellowship. Dea
 dline 16 August 2026\; interviews w/c 21 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: For
 ma\nLocation: London\, United Kingdom\; FormaHQ\, on site 10am-6pm.\nAward
 : GBP 36\,000 pro rata for four days a week (GBP 28\,800 actual). No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Fixed term\, 6 months\; 4 days per week\; 25 days h
 oliday plus bank holidays pro rata.\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/forms
 /d/e/1FAIpQLSfNSVKLQMxPqqwBbc9queqKvBCZqa7ET6cWcyFKOUXk1Ffarg/viewform?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfNSVKLQMxPqqwBbc9queqKvBCZqa7
 ET6cWcyFKOUXk1Ffarg/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:London\, United Kingdom\; FormaHQ\, on site 10am-6pm.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movida-labs-dance-technology-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: MOVIDA: Labs on Dance and Technology 2026/27
DESCRIPTION:MOVIDA is a Creative Europe co-funded consortium pairing academ
 ic institutions with dance centres across four European cities. Sixteen du
 os\, each made up of one dancer and one creative technologist\, are select
 ed across four themed labs: AI and accessibility in Bucharest\, AI and AR/
 VR in Dusseldorf\, AI and robotics in Lisbon\, and AI and mental health in
  Tallinn. Applicants are assessed on demonstrated capability in integratin
 g technology with live performance\, computational creativity\, and audien
 ce interaction. Participants selected for the labs receive fast-track cons
 ideration for the MOVIDA residencies running in 2027 and 2028.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: MOVIDA (Movement and Virtual Intelligence for the Development and Ac
 cessibility of Artists and Audiences)\nLocation: Four labs across Europe: 
 Bucharest (Romania)\, Dusseldorf (Germany)\, Lisbon and Montemor-o-Novo (P
 ortugal)\, and Tallinn (Estonia). Applications are accepted only from duos
  of one dancer and one creative technologist\; you cannot apply solo. Both
  members must reside in an EU or Creative Europe eligible country\, so Net
 herlands-based applicants qualify.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 gross per artist (EU
 R 2\,400 per duo)\, plus travel and accommodation covered\, plus a product
 ion budget of up to EUR 500 per duo. Accessibility and personal-assistance
  costs are covered by separate agreement. No application fee.\nDuration: N
 ine days per lab\, scheduled between 3 December 2026 and 11 February 2027\
 n\nMore: https://movida.dance/news/call-labs/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://movida.dance/news/call-labs/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Four labs across Europe: Bucharest (Romania)\, Dusseldorf (Germany
 )\, Lisbon and Montemor-o-Novo (Portugal)\, and Tallinn (Estonia). Applica
 tions are accepted only from duos of one dancer and one creative technolog
 ist\; you cannot apply solo. Both members must reside in an EU or Creative
  Europe eligible country\, so Netherlands-based applicants qualify.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:francoise-cite-internationale-arts-clinique-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Association Francoise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine x Cite 
 internationale des arts: Research and Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Launched in 2025\, this research and creation residency explore
 s the links between contemporary art\, psychiatry and the human sciences. 
 It is expressly not a therapeutic programme. It seeks artists whose practi
 ce resonates with the notion of the clinical\, meaning a situated approach
  that works closely with lived narratives and specific contexts\, and that
  engages with questions of care. The selected artist receives tailored sup
 port from Albertine de Galbert\, a clinical psychologist and exhibition cu
 rator\, including four to six working sessions\, alongside networking and 
 meeting time with programme partners. Outputs include an ongoing online jo
 urnal\, a mid-residency open studio\, and a closing presentation (exhibiti
 on\, public talk or publication) defined with the artist. Applications go 
 by email as a single PDF of no more than 15 MB to residence@francoiseartme
 mo.fr\, and require a two-page CV\, a ten-page portfolio\, a two-page stat
 ement of intent\, and a letter of recommendation from an institution or a 
 curator. A jury of four to six art and psychiatry specialists decides\, wi
 th results announced in September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Association Franc
 oise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine / Cite internationale des arts\nLocation:
  Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). Open to
  artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career or esta
 blished\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working in Fre
 nch or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current accessibil
 ity standards for people with disabilities.\nAward: Grant of EUR 1\,000 ne
 t of tax per month\, plus a furnished studio-apartment (20 to 35 sq m\, co
 mbining living and working space)\, international return travel to Paris a
 irports or stations\, travel insurance\, and capped research support again
 st receipts. Additional fees apply for accompanying persons. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Approximately 12 weeks\, 5 January to 26 March 2027\n\nM
 ore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associa
 tion-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associati
 on-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). 
 Open to artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career 
 or established\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working
  in French or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current acc
 essibility standards for people with disabilities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bloedel-reserve-creative-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Residency at Bloedel Reserve: Class of 2027
DESCRIPTION:Bloedel Reserve's residency programme exists to foster creative
  thinking inspired by nature and to explore the connection between humans 
 and the environment. It is open to professional and emerging artists\, com
 posers\, writers\, botanists\, landscape architects\, researchers and othe
 rs working on themes of nature and human connection to it. Residents get a
  three-week stay at a 140-acre internationally recognised public garden an
 d forest preserve\, housed in a small home hidden in the woods off the mai
 n paths. Note for non-US applicants: the funding is structured as expense 
 reimbursement rather than a stipend\, capped at USD 1\,000\, which for tra
 nsatlantic applicants is unlikely to cover airfare plus meals over three w
 eeks.\n\nOrganisation: Bloedel Reserve\nLocation: Bainbridge Island\, Wash
 ington\, USA\, between Seattle and the Kitsap Peninsula\, reachable by fer
 ry from Seattle or by car via the Kitsap Peninsula. Residents must be 21 o
 r older. International applicants are eligible but are funded differently 
 from domestic ones (see amount).\nAward: USD 22 application fee. Furnished
  private house on the grounds with linens\, stocked kitchen\, wi-fi\, laun
 dry and use of a smart car\; an electric piano is available. Domestic resi
 dents receive a USD 1\,000 stipend. International residents receive no sti
 pend and may instead submit up to USD 1\,000 of expenses for reimbursement
 . Residents pay for their own meals and their own travel to Bainbridge Isl
 and. There is no dedicated studio\; residents work in the house.\nDuration
 : Three weeks\; residents stay one at a time with no overlap\n\nMore: http
 s://bloedelreserve.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral#/login/program/88209
URL:https://bloedelreserve.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral#/login/program/88209
LOCATION:Bainbridge Island\, Washington\, USA\, between Seattle and the Kit
 sap Peninsula\, reachable by ferry from Seattle or by car via the Kitsap P
 eninsula. Residents must be 21 or older. International applicants are elig
 ible but are funded differently from domestic ones (see amount).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:klang-copenhagen-open-call-2027-music-movement@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211013Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Klang Copenhagen Avantgarde Music Festival: Open Call 202
 7\, MUSIC/MOVEMENT
DESCRIPTION:Klang\, Copenhagen's avantgarde music festival\, is seeking one
  to three projects at the intersection of experimental music and movement\
 , dance or choreography for its 2027 edition at Dansehallerne. Important c
 onstraint: the call is explicitly for ready-to-go projects\, not commissio
 ns or works in progress\, so the work must already be finished and product
 ion-ready. Submission is a one-page PDF covering artistic description\, bu
 dget overview\, bios\, duration and media links\, emailed to opencall@klan
 g.dk with 'Open Call 2027' in the subject line. The submission window runs
  1 July to 1 September 2026. The toaspern|moeller duo together with Klang 
 Festival review feasible submissions in September 2026\, with notification
  in October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Klang - Copenhagen Avantgarde Music Fes
 tival\nLocation: Dansehallerne\, Copenhagen\, Denmark. No nationality\, ag
 e or education restrictions are stated on the call page.\nAward: Klang aim
 s to cover production costs and performer fees. Travel and accommodation a
 re discussed case by case rather than guaranteed. No commission fee is off
 ered\, since the call seeks finished work rather than new creation. No app
 lication fee.\nDuration: Performance during Klang Festival 2027\, provisio
 nal dates 15 to 18 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.klang.dk/open-calls/open
 call2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.klang.dk/open-calls/opencall2027?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dansehallerne\, Copenhagen\, Denmark. No nationality\, age or educ
 ation restrictions are stated on the call page.
END:VEVENT
