SUMMARY:Deadline: The Grey Space in the Middle: State of States Open Call (
 The Hague)
DESCRIPTION:The Grey Space in the Middle in The Hague invites young transdi
 sciplinary makers based in the Netherlands whose practices engage with the
  intersections of art\, technology and society to submit an existing artwo
 rk for State of States\, a thematic exhibition diptych unfolding across tw
 o group shows (27 November - 6 December 2026 and 7 - 17 January 2027). The
  exhibition explores how artists locate themselves within a state\, politi
 cal or holistic\, informed by digital culture: statehood\, belonging\, dig
 italism\, inclusion/exclusion\, space-claiming and network-systems are the
  guiding keywords. Selected artists are divided into groups of five per ex
 hibition\; each receives a EUR 375 fee\, and can earn up to EUR 725 more f
 or co-organising and participating in a context programme developed collec
 tively between selection and build-up. APPLY with a description of the art
 work (max 500 words)\, up to 10 images\, recordings for moving image or so
 und work\, a portfolio and a link to socials/website. Deadline: 25 Septemb
 er 2026\, midnight.\n\nOrganisation: The Grey Space in the Middle\nLocatio
 n: The Hague\, Netherlands\nAward: EUR 375 artist fee per selected artist\
 , plus up to EUR 725 additional for co-organising and participating in the
  context programme (up to EUR 1\,100 total)\nDuration: Two group exhibitio
 ns: 27 November - 6 December 2026 and 7 - 17 January 2027\; side programme
  developed in the months before build-up\n\nMore: https://thegreyspace.net
 /open-call-state-of-states/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://thegreyspace.net/open-call-state-of-states/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands
