SUMMARY:Deadline: KTH Royal Institute of Technology: PhD\, Feminist AI Addr
 essing Gender-Based Violence
DESCRIPTION:Fully funded four-year PhD position (third-cycle subject: Infor
 mation and Communication Technology) on Feminist AI Addressing Gender-Base
 d Violence\, supervised by Associate Professor Amir Hossein Payberah at th
 e Department of Computing and Learning Systems. The project develops AI me
 thods that make online gender-based violence visible by detecting not only
  explicit abuse but also the structural silences and omissions that shape 
 digital narratives\, combining large language models\, NLP and machine lea
 rning to identify missing voices\, hidden patterns and gaps in institution
 al accountability. The doctoral student will develop novel ML models and e
 valuation methods\, construct large-scale datasets and knowledge graphs\, 
 collaborate with feminist organizations and civil society partners\, and p
 ublish in leading AI venues. ELIGIBILITY: a second-cycle (master's) degree
 \, or at least 240 higher education credits including 60 second-cycle cred
 its\, or substantially equivalent knowledge\, plus English equivalent to S
 wedish English B/6. APPLY via KTH's recruitment system (reference number P
 A-2026-2872) with certified copies of diplomas and grades\, CV\, an applic
 ation letter of maximum 2 pages\, representative publications or technical
  reports\, and contact details for two to three academic references. Deadl
 ine 24 September 2026 at midnight CEST.\n\nOrganisation: KTH Royal Institu
 te of Technology\, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (
 Department of Computing and Learning Systems)\nLocation: Stockholm\, Swede
 n\nAward: Fully funded\, full-time employed doctoral position with monthly
  salary according to KTH's collectively agreed doctoral student salary agr
 eement\, plus Swedish employee benefits. No application fee.\nDuration: Fo
 ur years full-time doctoral education (temporary employment renewed in inc
 rements\, initially up to one year then up to two years at a time)\; up to
  20 percent departmental duties such as teaching may be added. Start date 
 by agreement.\n\nMore: https://kth.varbi.com/what:job/jobID:963228/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kth.varbi.com/what:job/jobID:963228/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
